    "id": "a-future-left-open",
    "title": "A future left open",
    "lens": "book",
    "sources": [
      7,
      14
    ],
    "lines": [
      "The Tao of OMIS explores love without treating another person as a completed answer.",
      "Its standalone speculative triptych begins with finite people in a habitable dusk belt.",
      "Their attraction opens a question about influence, difference, and a future left unclaimed.",
      "The larger realms preserve that intimate question while changing its scale.",
      "Its vocabulary distinguishes a relationship's influence from quietly removing another person's possible futures.",
      "The stories keep that distinction embodied in people who can disagree and change."
    ],
