    "title": "Lives in the dusk belt",
    "lens": "content",
    "sources": [
      14
    ],
    "lines": [
      "Mara and Sio live within a habitable belt between intense heat and cold.",
      "Their world depends on practical forms of care, transport, and ecological attention.",
      "The relationship begins among finite people with different habits and responsibilities.",
      "Attraction does not settle how much one life may organize another.",
      "The setting gives dependence a material presence before the story expands its scale.",
      "Its intimacy matters because an uncertain future cannot be replaced by perfect agreement."
